QUESTION 3: (2p)
- the ORDER/Booking with status PENDING (not PAID yet) will be updated 'EXPIRED' after 30 days;
- please refer the sql below 
----------
UPDATE booking
SET status = 'EXPIRED'
WHERE status = 'PENDING' AND created_at < NOW() - INTERVAL 30 DAY;
----------
TASK: The DB has 100 million pending bookings expire everyday
Advice a plan step by step to solve this task that not affect to user's experience (slow db, slow app response, out of memory, app shutdown, db shutdown, etc) 
(all your knowlege about software, application desgin can be apply together to solve this task).

Answer: 
1. Indexing: 
problem is that we have to find all the pending bookings, then check if the booking is expired (>30 days) 
DB has 100M pendings bookings everyday, which means this is the heavy task for the system to scan and find all the pending bookings. 
That’s why I will index on status column (to make the booking be sorted according their status > all pending bookings are sorted into a group) which makes it easier for system to navigate to find all pendings. 
Next, I will put index on created_at as well.
The systems will look like: 

Paid…
Canceled…
Pending 
        01/01
        02/01
        03/01 ….
Then it will be much faster to find the date that exceeds 30 days. 

2. We also can proceed into small batches (10k or 50K) instead of 100M expired bookings at a time. If we try to process 100M expired bookings at the same time, the database has to handle a heavy load of work, then makes the whole system slow down and can lead to slow performance or long waiting time from customers’ searching experience. 


